  "body": "Add a post-then-read compare mode and conformance test suite across all 10 built-in milling posts (`crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`).\n\n## Scope\n- Post each `.cl` golden (`crates/app/tests/golden/*.cl`) through each of the 10 milling posts in `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (`fanuc`, `haas`, `sinumerik`, `heidenhain`, `mazak`, `tormach`, `grblhal`, `tinyg`, `doosan-dnm`, `carvera`).\n- Parse each posted NC output back through `camcraft-gcode` (#2217, #2219) using that post's dialect profile, `.mch`, and WCS origin.\n- Compare move endpoints, rapid/cut kinds, and arc chord deviations against the source `Toolpath` (allowing TinyG half-turn splits and Heidenhain vertical-arc chords).\n- Simulate both the source `Toolpath` and the read-back `Toolpath` in `camcraft_sim::stock_sim::Dexel` and assert matching stock surfaces within output rounding tolerance.\n- Check that `PostOutput::line_map` agrees with the reader's line map for each posted block.\n\nDepends on #2217 and #2219.\n\nDone means: All 10 built-in milling posts pass round-trip geometric, `Dexel` stock surface, and `PostOutput::line_map` comparison tests across the `.cl` golden fixtures.\n\nPart of #2213\n",
